WEBVTT

00:01.502 --> 00:04.420
♪ <i>It seems today that all you see</i> ♪

00:04.421 --> 00:07.706
♪ <i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i> ♪

00:07.707 --> 00:11.468
♪ <i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i> ♪

00:11.469 --> 00:14.471
♪ <i>On which we used to rely?</i> ♪

00:14.472 --> 00:18.249
♪ <i>Lucky there's a family guy</i> ♪

00:18.250 --> 00:21.646
♪ <i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i> ♪

00:21.647 --> 00:23.181
♪ <i>All the things that make us</i> ♪

00:23.182 --> 00:24.966
♪ <i>Laugh and cry</i> ♪

00:24.967 --> 00:30.646
♪ <i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i> ♪

00:36.872 --> 00:39.531
Rupert, remember
that very expensive bottle

00:39.532 --> 00:42.608
of coconut water I got
from Pressed Juicery in Newport

00:42.609 --> 00:44.318
that we were saving
for a special occasion?

00:44.319 --> 00:46.596
Well, I'm going to need you
to get two Dixie cups

00:46.597 --> 00:47.877
and open it!

00:47.878 --> 00:50.283
I got Busy Bee
for the second week in a row!

00:50.284 --> 00:53.211
Miss Debby said that I was
the best at sharing and helping.

00:53.212 --> 00:55.020
And she didn't even have to say that.

00:55.021 --> 00:57.441
She just had a cyst removed
from her ovary.

00:57.442 --> 00:59.718
You were right, Rupert.
I did exactly as you said.

00:59.719 --> 01:01.428
I just took it one day at a time

01:01.429 --> 01:03.746
and minded my own beeswax, and now look.

01:03.747 --> 01:05.890
Two weeks in a row.

01:05.891 --> 01:09.269
This is good for us.
This is very good for us.

01:09.270 --> 01:11.545
I know I wasn't originally supportive

01:11.546 --> 01:13.148
when you joined A.A., but I have to say,

01:13.149 --> 01:14.733
I've gotten something out of it, too.

01:14.734 --> 01:17.152
I mean, it works when you work,
so work it.

01:17.153 --> 01:19.070
Or, y-you know, h-however it goes.

01:19.071 --> 01:22.081
The point is, together,
we are unstoppable.

01:22.082 --> 01:23.743
I'm going for three weeks, Rupert.

01:23.744 --> 01:26.077
Nobody's ever gotten Busy Bee
three weeks in a row before,

01:26.078 --> 01:28.529
and with you by my side,
I know I can do it.

01:28.866 --> 01:31.157
You know, you look good.
I don't tell you that enough.

01:31.158 --> 01:34.276
I want to show you
how much I appreciate you.

01:34.832 --> 01:36.746
LOIS: Stewie, are you up there?

01:36.747 --> 01:39.048
(laughs) Her timing, am I right?

01:39.049 --> 01:40.818
- LOIS: Stewie?
- What?

01:40.819 --> 01:42.594
Oh, there you are, sweetie.

01:42.595 --> 01:44.272
You want some animal crackers?

01:44.273 --> 01:46.441
I just went to the market
and got a new crate.

01:46.442 --> 01:48.433
Ugh, can't you ever come back
from shopping

01:48.434 --> 01:49.934
without looking like
you were getting supplies

01:49.935 --> 01:51.235
for a refugee camp?

01:51.236 --> 01:53.195
They're downstairs if you want some.

01:53.196 --> 01:54.566
Get the hell out of here.

01:55.274 --> 01:57.892
You know what? I actually do
want some animal crackers, so...

01:57.893 --> 01:59.110
to be continued.

01:59.569 --> 02:00.923
The stuff is in the top drawer,

02:00.924 --> 02:02.642
so just, you know, get it ready.

02:10.714 --> 02:13.124
I'm going to do something
really nice for Rupert.

02:13.125 --> 02:15.594
Show him how much
he means to me, Annabelle.

02:16.495 --> 02:18.379
Oh, no, no. No, no,
I don't want you to kill anyone.

02:18.380 --> 02:20.128
- I'll let you know.
- There you are.

02:20.129 --> 02:21.223
What are you doing up here?

02:21.224 --> 02:23.843
Oh, hey, Bri.
I'm making a collage for Rupert.

02:23.844 --> 02:25.753
We've been firing
on all cylinders lately,

02:25.754 --> 02:27.607
and I just wanted
to let him know I care.

02:27.608 --> 02:28.700
That sounds stupid.

02:28.701 --> 02:30.350
Well, Annabelle doesn't think so.

02:30.351 --> 02:31.526
Right, Annabelle?

02:32.701 --> 02:34.446
PETER: Holy (bleep), what is that?!

02:35.514 --> 02:37.223
Wow, look at all these old photos.

02:37.224 --> 02:39.150
Aw, I was such a cute puppy.

02:39.151 --> 02:40.710
That's not you. That's Snuffles.

02:40.711 --> 02:42.862
- He got hit by a car.
- Oh, word?

02:42.863 --> 02:44.438
You want to see something upsetting?

02:44.439 --> 02:45.956
Look at this photo of Chris.

02:45.957 --> 02:48.701
He's, like, three years old,
and he's in a mobility scooter

02:48.702 --> 02:50.578
rolling around an oxygen tank.

02:50.579 --> 02:52.714
Wait. Is that Rupert?

02:53.407 --> 02:55.940
- Oh, yeah, I guess it is.
- What's he doing with Chris?

02:55.941 --> 02:58.319
Well, Rupert belonged to Chris
before he was yours.

02:58.320 --> 03:00.788
- Didn't you know that?
- No, I did not know that.

03:00.789 --> 03:02.058
Yeah, he was named Skippy.

03:02.059 --> 03:03.821
He had a different name?!

03:03.822 --> 03:05.659
Yeah, Skippy. Chris took him everywhere.

03:05.660 --> 03:07.728
- Used to sleep with him, too.
- You shut up!

03:07.729 --> 03:09.605
I think he was Peter's before that.

03:09.606 --> 03:11.540
Oh, God, this can't be happening.

03:11.541 --> 03:13.301
I thought Rupert was mine first,

03:13.302 --> 03:16.732
not some multigenerational
family dong koozie.

03:23.453 --> 03:25.872
We need to talk,<i> Skippy.</i>

03:26.373 --> 03:28.635
That's right,
I know all about you and Chris.

03:28.636 --> 03:30.535
Ah, ah, ah, don't.
Don't run out, don't run out.

03:30.536 --> 03:32.412
Look, just sit right there, please.

03:32.413 --> 03:33.872
I'm not angry, all right?

03:33.873 --> 03:35.874
I've j...
I've had a lot of time to think,

03:35.875 --> 03:38.620
and, well, look, I-I don't see

03:38.621 --> 03:40.903
why this has to change anything
between us.

03:40.904 --> 03:42.763
We both have a past.

03:42.764 --> 03:45.049
(high-pitched):
Hello, I'm a lady comedienne.

03:45.050 --> 03:47.460
I want to get on stage
and talk about my husband

03:47.461 --> 03:49.961
and how he leaves
the toilet seat up, et cetera.

03:49.962 --> 03:51.297
Yeah, you don't seem like a lady.

03:51.298 --> 03:53.215
Maybe a boy or a baby or something.

03:53.216 --> 03:54.634
I don't know, but you're no lady.

03:54.635 --> 03:55.918
How dare you, sir!

03:55.919 --> 03:57.920
Must I show you my genitalia

03:57.921 --> 04:00.179
in order to book a gig
at this establishment?

04:00.180 --> 04:02.751
- Because I will.
- Go on. Beat it, weirdo.

04:03.003 --> 04:04.709
(regular voice): Can I
just stick around a little bit

04:04.710 --> 04:07.037
so I can go up onstage
when you guys win an Emmy?

04:07.038 --> 04:09.239
♪ ♪

04:13.545 --> 04:15.439
Uh, I guess I'll hold it.

04:15.440 --> 04:18.124
I had something memorized,
and it all dumped out.

04:18.125 --> 04:20.251
Uh, thank you to the Academy

04:20.252 --> 04:22.220
and to all the viewers who watch.

04:27.209 --> 04:28.843
Is the light keeping you up?

04:29.274 --> 04:31.912
FYI, I'm more in love with Michelle,

04:31.913 --> 04:33.489
if that was even possible.

04:33.490 --> 04:36.417
Oh. Oh, you know,
I still have that headache.

04:36.418 --> 04:38.386
Well, if you want to go over
to Chris's room...

04:38.387 --> 04:41.055
I'm-I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

04:41.056 --> 04:43.149
I said I wouldn't do that, and I did it.

04:43.150 --> 04:45.300
I'm just gonna finish this chapter.

04:47.189 --> 04:48.595
I'm trying, Rupert.

04:48.596 --> 04:50.114
I really am. I want this to work.

04:50.115 --> 04:53.359
It's just that sometimes
I picture you in his bed, and...

04:53.360 --> 04:55.069
(breathes deeply)

04:55.070 --> 04:58.406
Anyway, big day tomorrow.
They're picking Busy Bee.

04:58.407 --> 04:59.850
I should get some sleep.

05:03.078 --> 05:05.045
(crying)

05:08.884 --> 05:10.510
I'm sorry.

05:10.511 --> 05:12.161
Nights are hard.

05:17.313 --> 05:18.377
Well...

05:20.612 --> 05:23.648
I didn't get it.
They gave Busy Bee to Frederick.

05:24.032 --> 05:25.184
Frederick!

05:25.651 --> 05:27.485
I'm not gonna hit you, so relax.

05:27.486 --> 05:29.136
Anyway, the point is

05:29.137 --> 05:31.030
it's not working anymore, Rupert.

05:31.031 --> 05:33.515
I can't focus. I can't concentrate.

05:33.516 --> 05:35.417
Clearly, my work is suffering.

05:35.418 --> 05:38.680
Look, we're both adults.
We can split custody of Simon.

05:39.213 --> 05:40.665
I guess I'd better tell him.

05:40.666 --> 05:42.250
- Simon?
- (beeps)

05:42.251 --> 05:45.199
You know Mommy and Daddy
love you very much.

05:45.200 --> 05:46.395
(beeps twice)

05:46.396 --> 05:48.716
But Mommy and Daddy
need some time apart.

05:48.717 --> 05:49.749
(sustained low beep)

05:49.750 --> 05:53.103
Simon. Simon. Simon.

05:57.199 --> 05:58.317
Knock, knock.

05:58.318 --> 06:00.484
Stewie, can you see who's there?

06:00.485 --> 06:03.195
- What?
- Someone was knocking at the door.

06:03.196 --> 06:05.431
It-it was me.
I just went "knock, knock."

06:05.432 --> 06:06.742
There they are again.

06:06.743 --> 06:08.010
I don't even know how to process that,

06:08.011 --> 06:09.130
so I'm just gonna crack on.

06:09.131 --> 06:11.474
I have somebody here
that would like to see you.

06:11.475 --> 06:13.895
- Your teddy bear.
- You don't have to be coy.

06:13.896 --> 06:15.555
I know he was yours first.

06:15.556 --> 06:19.428
And, well, I want you to have...
Skippy back.

06:19.429 --> 06:21.797
I know you're going to try
and stop me, but hear me...

06:21.798 --> 06:24.164
- Okay.
- Oh. Great.

06:24.165 --> 06:25.869
Then I'll just leave him here.

06:26.323 --> 06:28.313
I hope you're both
very happy together, Chris.

06:28.874 --> 06:30.715
He belongs with you, not me.

06:31.168 --> 06:33.426
Well, I should get back to my book.

06:33.427 --> 06:35.395
That's a clock, but okay.

06:40.046 --> 06:41.917
This is just one night, got it?

06:41.918 --> 06:43.135
Now, I'm going to call you Rupert.

06:43.136 --> 06:44.395
You okay with that?

06:44.396 --> 06:46.222
And tomorrow, nothing happened.

06:46.223 --> 06:48.149
By the way, I have a Sleep Number bed.

06:48.150 --> 06:51.611
But don't worry, I don't
use it for sexual purposes.

06:51.612 --> 06:53.820
(motor whirring)

06:56.800 --> 06:58.025
What do you think of that?

06:58.026 --> 07:00.077
That something you can work with?

07:07.777 --> 07:10.755
(yawning)

07:10.756 --> 07:13.482
Well, looks like someone was up late.

07:13.483 --> 07:15.450
Yeah, I tend to sleep a little longer

07:15.451 --> 07:18.562
when I'm resting under
a big, furry bear.

07:18.563 --> 07:22.573
Oh, no! They's doin'
gay jokes without me.

07:22.574 --> 07:24.793
Shh, shh, shh, shh. It's okay.

07:24.794 --> 07:26.240
You're part of it now.

07:31.309 --> 07:33.152
God, you're sexy.

07:33.370 --> 07:35.988
What are you looking at?!
I told you that was one night!

07:35.989 --> 07:38.098
Now get out. I called you an Uber.

07:38.099 --> 07:40.266
I'll know if you went further
than your house.

07:42.015 --> 07:43.445
- Hey, what are you doin'?
- Oh, hey, Bri.

07:43.446 --> 07:46.124
I was just putting some product
in my hair, you know.

07:46.125 --> 07:49.014
Yeah, this looks good.
Give it a little height.

07:49.015 --> 07:51.712
Let everyone know Stewie's
back on the market.

07:51.713 --> 07:53.155
I heard that on<i> Friends.</i>

07:53.156 --> 07:55.007
Did you know they're all 60 now?

07:55.008 --> 07:57.017
I knew Courteney Cox was.

07:57.018 --> 07:59.714
So, how you doing with Rupert
gone and everything?

07:59.715 --> 08:01.814
Are you kidding? I'm fantastic!

08:01.815 --> 08:04.084
He was kind of holding me back,
if I'm being honest.

08:04.085 --> 08:07.611
It's time I got out there again.
I've had one bear my whole life.

08:07.612 --> 08:10.155
- That's not normal.
- Nothing about you is normal.

08:10.156 --> 08:13.171
I mean, I've already wasted a
whole year of my life with him.

08:13.172 --> 08:15.160
There's only been a year of your life.

08:15.161 --> 08:17.162
You know, all of your responses
have been very similar,

08:17.163 --> 08:18.747
so you might want to nip that
in the bud.

08:18.748 --> 08:21.750
Look, the truth is, things got
a bit stale between us.

08:21.751 --> 08:23.877
There wasn't one part of Rupert's body

08:23.878 --> 08:25.787
that I didn't know by heart.

08:25.788 --> 08:27.381
None of it excites me anymore.

08:27.382 --> 08:29.825
Well, do you want me to
keep an eye on Rupert for you?

08:29.826 --> 08:31.234
Make sure he's doing okay?

08:31.235 --> 08:33.466
No need. I turned him into a nanny cam.

08:33.467 --> 08:35.664
- A nanny cam?
- Yeah, I put it inside him.

08:35.665 --> 08:37.969
Deep. It's inside him now.

08:37.970 --> 08:40.502
I-I don't know how to respond
that won't sound similar

08:40.503 --> 08:43.397
to other responses I've made,
so just, uh, continue.

08:43.398 --> 08:45.607
Right. Well, whenever Chris
and Rupert interact,

08:45.608 --> 08:48.668
ten minutes later, I'll get a
chime notification on my phone,

08:48.669 --> 08:50.279
and I can pull up the video.

08:50.280 --> 08:51.388
Why is there a delay?

08:51.389 --> 08:52.845
Why can't you get the video immediately?

08:52.846 --> 08:54.772
I don't know.
Why can't you poop on a toilet?

08:54.773 --> 08:56.000
- Fair.
- (phone chimes)

08:56.001 --> 08:57.411
Ah, it's chiming, it's chiming.

08:57.412 --> 08:59.307
Okay, okay, calm down, just calm down.

08:59.308 --> 09:00.700
(breathes deeply)

09:00.701 --> 09:01.841
Now, what do we have?

09:03.949 --> 09:07.671
Oops. Sorry, Skippy.

09:07.672 --> 09:10.174
(gasps) Are you seeing what I'm seeing?

09:10.175 --> 09:11.758
Is Chris wearing a nicotine patch?

09:11.759 --> 09:13.802
You know what, it's just like I said.

09:13.803 --> 09:16.473
He and Chris go together,
like peaches and cream.

09:16.848 --> 09:18.988
Peaches. Peaches, I'm sorry.

09:18.989 --> 09:21.159
Damn it. You could've at least
given me some warning.

09:21.160 --> 09:23.144
At least a-a shoulder tap.

09:23.145 --> 09:24.529
I know, you're right.

09:24.530 --> 09:26.381
It's just that you're so beautiful,

09:26.382 --> 09:28.792
I can't control myself sometimes.

09:28.793 --> 09:30.777
Aw, I can't stay mad at you.

09:30.778 --> 09:32.003
How about a kiss?

09:32.004 --> 09:35.223
(chuckles): No-ho-ho-ho. Oh, no.

09:39.270 --> 09:43.006
(forced laughter)

09:43.007 --> 09:45.842
I'm sorry, was that loud?
Sorry, everyone.

09:45.843 --> 09:48.504
We're being loud. Oh, this is Anton.

09:48.505 --> 09:50.923
Stewie, let Mommy help you
into your high chair.

09:50.924 --> 09:53.513
Well, I am a little wobbly today.

09:53.514 --> 09:55.026
It's your fault, you know.

09:55.027 --> 09:57.804
Stop it, we're with my family.

09:57.805 --> 09:59.627
Easy. You're pinching my pits.

09:59.628 --> 10:02.158
God, it's like being picked up
with lobster claws.

10:02.159 --> 10:03.769
We hate her, by the way.

10:03.770 --> 10:06.896
Ah, I see you got my text
to bring Rupert to dinner.

10:06.897 --> 10:09.274
You're looking well. And this is Anton.

10:09.275 --> 10:11.694
He's in the touring company
of<i> Dear Evan Hansen.</i>

10:12.137 --> 10:13.987
My, aren't we all very modern?

10:13.988 --> 10:17.797
He's just here 'cause I got gum
on him and he stuck to my hand.

10:18.643 --> 10:20.269
Okay, that's sickening.

10:20.270 --> 10:22.871
Remember when that bear
used to be yours, Chris?

10:22.872 --> 10:25.316
Oh, you used to take him
with you every...

10:25.317 --> 10:27.225
You shut your mouth,
you hear me? Shut it!

10:27.226 --> 10:29.278
Oh, someone's tired.

10:29.279 --> 10:31.229
Brian, you want to put the baby down?

10:31.230 --> 10:32.773
Okay, yeah, he is a little fussy.

10:32.774 --> 10:35.275
I'll take him upstairs. Come on, Stewie.

10:35.276 --> 10:37.620
Brian, he's not in<i> Evan Hansen.</i>

10:37.621 --> 10:39.538
He's a male prostitute.

10:39.539 --> 10:41.307
Very cheap.

10:45.645 --> 10:48.488
Please tell me Rupert looked
fat, Brian. I'm begging you.

10:48.489 --> 10:51.024
He's a stuffed bear...
He-he looked enormous.

10:51.025 --> 10:53.251
Yeah, I thought so, too.
Puffy, you know?

10:53.252 --> 10:55.638
Glug, glug, glug.
Someone's back on the sauce.

10:55.639 --> 10:57.348
(phone chimes)

10:57.349 --> 11:00.125
Goodnight, Skippy.

11:00.126 --> 11:02.761
Just a warning, I had some
bad experiences at camp,

11:02.762 --> 11:05.938
so now I sleep with one eye open.

11:09.936 --> 11:12.153
(raspy breathing)

11:17.202 --> 11:20.329
I can't believe it, Brian.
I've been forgotten.

11:20.330 --> 11:22.498
I can't take it anymore!
It's eating me alive!

11:22.499 --> 11:23.949
What are you gonna to do?

11:23.950 --> 11:25.692
I-I need to take a trip.

11:25.693 --> 11:27.744
You know? Go on a spiritual journey.

11:27.745 --> 11:30.214
Find out who Stewie is
without Rupert, you know?

11:30.215 --> 11:32.733
I just have to get
an Uber to the airport.

11:32.734 --> 11:36.369
Wait... my Uber rating is 4.2?!
What happened?

11:36.370 --> 11:38.471
(classical music playing)

11:41.709 --> 11:43.060
(tires screech)

11:43.748 --> 11:47.463
_

11:47.464 --> 11:49.672
(Indonesian music playing)

11:52.270 --> 11:55.255
Excuse me, I'm in Bali
on a spiritual journey

11:55.256 --> 11:56.590
but I seem to have mistakenly wandered

11:56.591 --> 11:58.409
on to the heavy people beach.

11:58.410 --> 12:01.352
Do you happen to know where
the thin, attractive beach is?

12:01.353 --> 12:04.015
Thank you and good luck with
whatever's going on with you.

12:08.786 --> 12:12.572
Hey. You should've seen the pigs
where I was before.

12:13.024 --> 12:14.942
I'm only wearing a Speedo
because that's what they wear

12:14.943 --> 12:16.501
in this country.

12:16.502 --> 12:18.429
(chuckles): If I...
if I weren't wearing one,

12:18.430 --> 12:20.872
then I would stand out, right?

12:20.873 --> 12:22.659
I'm on a spiritual journey. You?

12:23.476 --> 12:26.018
Oh, you don't speak English. Cool.

12:30.625 --> 12:34.127
Rupert? Rupert, is that you?!
You followed me!

12:34.128 --> 12:35.879
This can be a second chance for us.

12:35.880 --> 12:38.907
Let's put everything behind... Oh... oh.

12:38.908 --> 12:40.409
Sorry, I'm-I'm so embarrassed.

12:40.410 --> 12:43.454
You-you look like... an old friend.

12:43.455 --> 12:45.697
He lives with someone else now.

12:45.698 --> 12:47.741
Well, sorry.

12:48.309 --> 12:49.918
You've got to get a grip
on yourself, Stewie.

12:49.919 --> 12:52.240
Put Rupert and Chris out of your head.

12:52.730 --> 12:54.498
Excuse me, where are your parents?

12:54.499 --> 12:57.509
Oh. I-I don't... I'm-I'm-I'm like...

12:57.510 --> 13:00.071
I'm like a... I'm-I'm like a baby guy.

13:00.928 --> 13:03.654
_

13:04.283 --> 13:07.952
(Italian music playing)

13:10.873 --> 13:12.799
Mm. So anyway,

13:12.800 --> 13:16.655
so I'm-I'm Eat Gay Loving it
and it's-it's going great.

13:16.656 --> 13:18.947
And I... Yeah, I finally feel

13:18.948 --> 13:20.783
like I'm getting my life together again

13:20.784 --> 13:22.301
af-after the breakup.

13:24.120 --> 13:27.658
Oh, my God, oh, this pasta...
This is amazing.

13:27.659 --> 13:29.022
This is amazing. I'm... You know what?

13:29.023 --> 13:30.959
I'm never going to fit into
that Speedo again.

13:30.960 --> 13:33.353
(chuckles) Hmm? I will?

13:33.354 --> 13:35.063
Aw.

13:35.064 --> 13:37.800
Th-The whole point of-of this journal...

13:37.801 --> 13:39.802
spirit... spiritual journal...

13:39.803 --> 13:42.087
j-journey, spiritual journey...

13:42.088 --> 13:43.927
Why-why was that so hard?

13:45.591 --> 13:48.239
...is to be Stewie, you know?

13:48.240 --> 13:49.911
Love Stewie.

13:49.912 --> 13:52.205
Love me. You know, love me.

13:52.206 --> 13:53.932
Stop-stop pouring. Stop pouring.
I can't...

13:53.933 --> 13:56.568
I can't keep track of how
much I'm drinking. Thank you.

13:56.569 --> 13:58.570
Thank you.

13:58.571 --> 14:01.818
Thank you so much
for taking me out, guys.

14:02.759 --> 14:05.720
_

14:06.345 --> 14:08.665
♪ ♪

14:09.015 --> 14:12.143
_

14:28.017 --> 14:29.834
The retreat is now finished.

14:29.835 --> 14:32.384
I hope you have found the peace
you have come here looking for.

14:32.663 --> 14:35.807
Wow. I have so much clarity now.

14:35.808 --> 14:37.705
I know how I'm going to move on.

14:38.169 --> 14:40.770
I have to kill Chris
and Rupert right away.

14:40.771 --> 14:42.480
I guess that means I'll miss that taping

14:42.481 --> 14:44.533
of<i> Deepak Choprah Winfrey.</i>

14:44.759 --> 14:46.608
Everyone, check your seats!

14:47.553 --> 14:49.395
You get diarrhea!

14:49.396 --> 14:50.914
- (cheering)
- And you get diarrhea!

14:50.915 --> 14:52.875
And you get diarrhea!

14:52.876 --> 14:55.543
Everyone's getting diarrhea...!

15:02.001 --> 15:03.455
So, how was the trip?

15:03.456 --> 15:05.112
Um, fabulous.

15:05.113 --> 15:06.780
Well, I have to say, you do look better.

15:06.781 --> 15:08.198
I feel better, Bri.

15:08.199 --> 15:10.367
It was the best thing
I could have done for myself.

15:10.368 --> 15:12.244
And you're good
with Chris and Rupert now?

15:12.245 --> 15:13.662
Oh, yeah, I'm so good.

15:13.663 --> 15:15.705
Yeah, I acted like a real tool before.

15:15.706 --> 15:17.374
You know, I'm actually
gonna make it up to them.

15:17.375 --> 15:18.708
Well, I'm so glad to hear that, Stewie.

15:18.709 --> 15:19.717
What are you gonna do?

15:19.718 --> 15:22.087
I've got something
super special planned.

15:22.088 --> 15:24.256
Well, I'm happy you're back.
I missed you.

15:24.257 --> 15:27.467
I'm happy I'm back, too.
Oh, and you can skip India.

15:27.468 --> 15:29.035
Huh. Really?

15:34.492 --> 15:36.293
How old is this place?

15:36.519 --> 15:38.736
That black-and-white TV
still has a white dot

15:38.737 --> 15:41.005
from when they turned it off
six years ago.

15:46.813 --> 15:48.191
Hey, Chris, just checking to see

15:48.192 --> 15:50.107
how long before you and Rupert get here.

15:50.780 --> 15:52.319
Okay, see you soon, pal.

15:52.320 --> 15:54.919
Hope you're hungry. I'm making
something really special.

15:55.329 --> 15:58.048
Goodness, I haven't done
a maniacal laugh in a while.

15:58.049 --> 15:59.318
Hope I'm not rusty.

15:59.319 --> 16:03.228
(forced laughter)

16:03.229 --> 16:05.112
That's perfect.

16:12.723 --> 16:14.713
Takeout's fine, he'll never know.

16:14.714 --> 16:16.800
I don't know why I said
I was making dinner.

16:16.801 --> 16:18.467
I'm committing a murder,
I should've realized

16:18.468 --> 16:20.035
I wouldn't also want to cook.

16:21.981 --> 16:24.800
They're here! I can't wait for
Rupert to see how good I look.

16:24.801 --> 16:27.134
It'll be the last thing he sees.

16:29.663 --> 16:32.001
- Hi, guys!
- Hey, Stewie,

16:32.002 --> 16:34.135
I brought Rupert, just like you said.

16:34.136 --> 16:35.644
Yes, and nothing else, I see.

16:35.645 --> 16:36.961
What do you mean?

16:36.962 --> 16:38.852
Like dessert or a bottle of wine.

16:38.853 --> 16:40.482
It's customary to bring a hostess gift

16:40.483 --> 16:43.020
- when invited to dinner.
- I didn't know.

16:43.021 --> 16:45.749
Everyone knows that
but whatever. Sit, sit, sit!

16:45.750 --> 16:47.072
Well, how is everything?

16:47.073 --> 16:48.807
Oh, Anton couldn't make it.

16:48.808 --> 16:50.158
Poor thing's brother has AIDS.

16:50.159 --> 16:53.049
Anyhoo, it is so good
to see the two of you.

16:53.050 --> 16:55.787
This is weird. Why am I here?

16:55.788 --> 16:57.407
For dinner. Here.

16:57.408 --> 16:58.679
What are we having?

16:58.680 --> 17:01.777
Uh... pasta... primavera.

17:02.955 --> 17:04.439
Who made this?

17:04.440 --> 17:06.609
I made it.
I told you I was making dinner.

17:06.610 --> 17:08.283
It tastes like it's from a store.

17:08.284 --> 17:10.203
Well, it's not! You know,
you're making this thing

17:10.204 --> 17:12.113
a whole lot easier.

17:12.114 --> 17:13.615
What whole thing?

17:13.616 --> 17:15.116
I thought I could live with the idea

17:15.117 --> 17:17.306
of you and Rupert together,
I-I really did.

17:17.307 --> 17:18.893
I see the way he looks at you.

17:18.894 --> 17:20.699
He used to look at me like that.

17:20.700 --> 17:22.619
Knowing he loves you and not me,

17:22.620 --> 17:25.297
it's too painful and I now realize...

17:25.886 --> 17:27.919
Sorry, that's been bugging me all day.

17:27.920 --> 17:30.894
I now realize the only way
I can go on with my life

17:30.895 --> 17:32.589
is by ending yours.

17:32.590 --> 17:34.582
You're planning on killing me?

17:34.583 --> 17:36.884
Oh, my God, you poisoned my food?

17:36.885 --> 17:38.389
That's why it tastes so funny!

17:38.390 --> 17:39.889
It's from a good store!

17:39.890 --> 17:41.391
I thought you said you made it.

17:41.392 --> 17:43.809
I did m... All right, look,
we're-we're getting off track here.

17:43.810 --> 17:45.609
How much longer do I have?

17:45.610 --> 17:47.485
There's no poison in the food, Chris.

17:47.486 --> 17:49.442
Although, that actually would
have been smart, wouldn't it?

17:49.443 --> 17:50.798
Damn it. I'm sorry,

17:50.799 --> 17:52.929
I-I haven't done this whole
Hitchcock thing before.

17:52.930 --> 17:55.871
This hasn't been very Hitchcockian.

17:55.872 --> 17:57.110
Oh, that you know.

17:57.111 --> 17:58.476
Then I'm just gonna leave.

17:58.477 --> 18:00.023
A-And why should I bring a gift

18:00.024 --> 18:02.369
- if you were gonna kill me?
- Etiquette?

18:02.370 --> 18:04.474
Look, I'm afraid
I can't let you go, Chris.

18:04.475 --> 18:06.209
(grunts)

18:06.210 --> 18:08.274
- (gasps)
- Peter, what is it?

18:08.275 --> 18:10.237
I forgot to record <i>Young Sheldon.</i>

18:13.100 --> 18:16.623
Oh, we got a nice evening
for this. Nice evening.

18:16.624 --> 18:17.854
It's like the perfect temperature.

18:17.855 --> 18:19.586
I don't even need a sweater.

18:19.587 --> 18:21.624
Wait. What are you doing, Stewie?

18:21.625 --> 18:24.050
You can turn around right now
and go back home.

18:24.051 --> 18:25.269
This is your brother.

18:25.270 --> 18:26.237
(both grunt)

18:26.238 --> 18:28.497
♪ ♪

18:28.498 --> 18:30.890
This is exactly how it
happened in the movie!

18:30.891 --> 18:33.029
How can you say this
isn't like Hitchcock?!

18:33.030 --> 18:35.010
This is from <i>The Talented Mr. Ripley.</i>

18:35.011 --> 18:36.781
It's not a Hitchcock film!

18:36.782 --> 18:38.079
- It's not?
- No.

18:38.080 --> 18:40.409
It was directed by Anthony Minghella.

18:40.410 --> 18:42.159
(choking): But isn't it a remake?

18:42.160 --> 18:44.659
Of a French film! (cries out)

18:44.660 --> 18:46.649
Oh! (grunts)

18:52.138 --> 18:54.114
This is all because of you, Rupert.

18:54.115 --> 18:55.589
You broke my heart.

18:55.590 --> 18:57.650
- And now it's your turn.
- (phone chimes)

18:58.850 --> 19:00.678
<i>Okay, Rupert, so remember,</i>

19:00.679 --> 19:01.706
<i>we sit through a nice dinner</i>

19:01.707 --> 19:04.235
<i>and then you go back with Stewie.</i>

19:04.236 --> 19:06.912
<i>Because I love my
little brother, and so do you.</i>

19:06.913 --> 19:08.963
<i>You guys belong together.</i>

19:10.174 --> 19:12.825
So... you do love me.

19:12.826 --> 19:15.577
Oh, Rupert, I love you so much!

19:15.578 --> 19:17.979
And I didn't want to say it
because I-I didn't know if you

19:17.980 --> 19:21.909
were going to say it back and
oh, what a fool I've... Chris!

19:21.910 --> 19:24.436
♪ ♪

19:27.341 --> 19:30.693
(panting, grunting)

19:35.658 --> 19:38.351
(grunting)

19:38.352 --> 19:40.536
(grunting continues)

19:45.209 --> 19:47.418
♪ ♪

19:51.519 --> 19:53.419
Come on, he's my brother.

19:55.127 --> 19:57.012
Well, you have to use a little tongue.

19:57.013 --> 19:59.014
(coughing)

19:59.015 --> 20:01.158
(gasping)

20:02.535 --> 20:05.245
Chris, are you all right?
Please, say something!

20:05.246 --> 20:07.789
I don't think Jordan Peele
has the talent

20:07.790 --> 20:09.789
we've attributed to him.

20:09.790 --> 20:12.168
Because of the lake water,

20:12.169 --> 20:15.755
uh, I said some things
that I did not mean.

20:15.756 --> 20:20.283
Jordan Peele is our greatest
living filmmaker, and visionary,

20:20.284 --> 20:22.844
both in comedy and in drama.

20:22.845 --> 20:25.068
There is nothing he can't do.

20:25.520 --> 20:30.309
(distorted): Good.
Now let's make some twin porn.

20:30.310 --> 20:32.898
Hit me again and you got a deal.

20:41.375 --> 20:43.079
Hey, sleepyhead.

20:43.080 --> 20:45.789
- Stewie.
- How ya feelin', pal?

20:45.790 --> 20:47.789
Uh... Okay.

20:47.790 --> 20:49.409
Do you remember what happened?

20:50.516 --> 20:53.218
- No.
- That's the right answer.

20:53.219 --> 20:54.627
Well, you have a lovely day

20:54.628 --> 20:56.088
and we'll see you when you get home.

20:57.615 --> 20:59.340
I think we can get
a heart from this kid.

20:59.341 --> 21:00.718
Uhp, nope, he's up.